From 4e5cbb5d730bacc7e4e516ceac870bf165e812a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Caleb J. Westfall" <calebwestfall1989@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:40:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] SOTA-1: executable competitor benchmark infrastructure,
 joint-drift research theorems, availability and novelty report

- bench/: canonical case format (labels rejected in cases), EPLA/ProofNetVerif ingestion with
  source labels kept apart, custodian sealing (group-disjoint pilot/primary, salted SHA-256 label
  commitments), external CPU limit (prlimit) + process-group RSS watchdog, adapters for ProofScope
  v1.2 (with a with_reducible-rfl meaning-preservation check), SemantEq (native pair format) and
  BEq+ (unmodified upstream function), pre-registered certified/native outcome mapping, scoring with
  Clopper-Pearson, group-clustered bootstrap, exact McNemar + Holm.
- .github/workflows/competitor-benchmark.yml: infrastructure tests, research-theorem axiom check and
  fresh replay, candidate pools, sharded per-system runs, completeness table; scoring only after the
  custodian releases gold.
- research/joint_drift/JointDrift.lean: 7 theorems (6 axiom-free, 1 standard) for joint
  assumption+conclusion drift, incl. certified logical difference and a non-compositionality result.
- docs/sota1/: availability matrix, corpus specification (EPLA facts, vendor-home strata),
  adjudication instructions, novelty analysis (FormalRx-CC is the closest prior art), status
  classification (engineering result; no comparative result exists), amendments A1-A6, errata.

No benchmark has been run; no labels exist; no superiority is claimed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
